          hint: "G3 to G6: =SUMIF($B$2:$B$11,F3,$D$2:$D$11) and so on; SUMIF simply skips the blank amounts. G7 is the sum of G3:G6, G8 divides it by G2, G9 is (G5+G6)/G7. G10 needs two SUMIFS, one for each failure category, both with Line = Blister. G11 uses COUNTBLANK on D2:D11. G12: =IF(G9>0.5,\"Invest in prevention\",\"Keep plan\").",
