  quiz: {
    id: "qt-m1-quiz",
    title: "Module 1 Quiz",
    passPct: 70,
    questions: [
      { id: "q1", question: "Which of these is an appraisal cost?", options: ["Training operators on a new filler", "Calibrating the lab micrometers", "Scrapping cracked castings", "Paying a customer penalty for a late recall"], answer: 1, explain: "Calibration keeps inspection equipment accurate, so it is part of the cost of checking: appraisal." },
      { id: "q2", question: "A roofing sheet meets every dimension on its drawing but rusts within a year near the coast in Douala. Which view of quality does it fail?", options: ["Conformance to requirements", "Appraisal", "Internal failure", "Fitness for use"], answer: 3, explain: "It conforms to the drawing but does not do what the customer needs in real conditions, so it is not fit for use." },
      { id: "q3", question: "Which instrument best suits checking 800 bores per shift as simply pass or fail?", options: ["A go/no-go plug gauge", "A CMM", "A hardness tester", "A surface plate"], answer: 0, explain: "A plug gauge gives a fast and reliable pass or fail decision without reading a value." },
      { id: "q4", question: "Under ISO 9001 clause 7.1.5, what must you do when a caliper is found out of calibration?", options: ["Only replace it with a new one", "Assess whether results obtained with it since its last good check are still valid, and act if they are not", "Destroy its calibration record", "Nothing, if no customer has complained"], answer: 1, explain: "The standard asks you to check whether earlier measurement results were affected and to take action if needed." },
      { id: "q5", question: "In the PDCA cycle, internal audits and management review belong to which step?", options: ["Plan", "Do", "Check", "Act"], answer: 2, explain: "They are part of clause 9, performance evaluation, which is the Check step." },
      { id: "q6", question: "A completed and signed first-piece inspection sheet is a…", options: ["Procedure", "Work instruction", "Form", "Record"], answer: 3, explain: "The blank sheet is a form; once filled in and signed, it becomes a record: evidence of what was done." },
      { id: "q7", question: "What is the difference between rework and repair?", options: ["Rework brings the product fully back to the requirement; repair makes it usable although it still does not meet the original requirement", "There is no difference", "Repair is always cheaper than rework", "Rework needs customer approval, repair never does"], answer: 0, explain: "After rework the product conforms. After repair it is fit for use but still deviates, so a concession is usually needed." },
      { id: "q8", question: "Parts produced since the last good check are suspect. What is the correct first action?", options: ["Ship them and inspect the next batch more carefully", "Hold and tag the whole suspect quantity and move it to quarantine", "Scrap all of them at once", "Rework them without recording anything"], answer: 1, explain: "Containment comes first: hold everything that may be affected, then report and decide on a disposition." },
    ],
  },
